{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "from typing import Iterable, Tuple, List\n\ndef find_tuples(tuples: Iterable[Tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples where all elements are divisible by k from a list of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuples: An iterable of tuples of integers.\n        k: Non-zero integer divisor.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of tuples from the input where every element is divisible by k.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If k is zero.\n        TypeError: If elements of tuples are not tuples or their items are not ints.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(k, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"k must be an integer\")\n    if k == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be non-zero\")\n\n    result: List[Tuple[int, ...]] = []\n    for idx, t in enumerate(tuples):\n        if not isinstance(t, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Item at index {idx} is not a tuple: {t!r}\")\n        if not all(isinstance(e, int) for e in t):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements of tuple at index {idx} must be integers: {t!r}\")\n        if all((element % k == 0) for element in t):\n            result.append(t)\n    return result"}
