{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "def is_Diff(number):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    The input is normalized to a string of digits, and then the alternating sum is computed.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert the number to a string and strip whitespace.\n    s = str(number).strip()\n\n    # Handle optional leading '+' or '-' signs by discarding them for the divisibility check.\n    if s.startswith('+'):\n        s = s[1:]\n    elif s.startswith('-'):\n        s = s[1:]\n\n    # Remove leading zeros, ensuring '0' remains if the number is zero.\n    digits_only_s = s.lstrip('0') or '0'\n\n    total = 0\n    # Compute the alternating sum of digits from right to left.\n    for idx, char_digit in enumerate(reversed(digits_only_s), start=1):\n        digit = ord(char_digit) - ord('0')  # Convert character digit to integer.\n        if idx % 2 == 1:  # Digits at odd positions (1st, 3rd, etc. from right) are added.\n            total += digit\n        else:             # Digits at even positions (2nd, 4th, etc. from right) are subtracted.\n            total -= digit\n\n    # A number is divisible by 11 if its alternating sum (absolute value) is divisible by 11.\n    return abs(total) % 11 == 0"}
