{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using dynamic programming.\n    The sequence is defined as a(1)=1, a(2)=1, a(n)=a(a(n-1))+a(n-a(n-1)) for n>2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return 0\n\n    arr = [0] * (n + 1)\n\n    if n >= 1:\n        arr[1] = 1\n    if n >= 2:\n        arr[2] = 1\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        arr[i] = arr[arr[i - 1]] + arr[i - arr[i - 1]]\n\n    return arr[n]"}
