{"task_id": "Mbpp/93", "solution": "def power(a, b):\n    # Calculates 'a' to the power 'b' using the exponentiation by squaring algorithm.\n    # This implementation assumes 'a' is a real number and 'b' is an integer.\n\n    if b == 0:\n        return 1.0\n\n    current_a = float(a)\n    current_b = abs(b)\n    result = 1.0\n\n    while current_b > 0:\n        if current_b % 2 == 1:\n            result *= current_a\n        current_a *= current_a\n        current_b //= 2\n\n    if b < 0:\n        return 1.0 / result\n    else:\n        return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is undulating, meaning its digits strictly alternate between two distinct values,\n    and the number has at least three digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        number = abs(number)\n\n    if number == 0:\n        digits = [0]\n    else:\n        digits = []\n        n = number\n        while n > 0:\n            digits.append(n % 10)\n            n //= 10\n        digits.reverse()\n\n    if len(digits) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    first_digit = digits[0]\n    second_digit = digits[1]\n\n    if first_digit == second_digit:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(len(digits)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index, should match first_digit\n            if digits[i] != first_digit:\n                return False\n        else:  # Odd index, should match second_digit\n            if digits[i] != second_digit:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
