{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of an integer using Brian Kernighan's algorithm.\"\"\"\n    x = abs(n)\n    count = 0\n    while x:\n        x &= (x - 1)\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/227", "solution": "def min_of_three(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum of three numbers.\n    The result is always returned as a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert inputs to float to ensure consistent comparison and return type\n    fa = float(a)\n    fb = float(b)\n    fc = float(c)\n\n    if fa <= fb and fa <= fc:\n        return fa\n    if fb <= fc:\n        return fb\n    return fc"}
