{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of sequences of length n such that each element\n    is a positive integer <= m and >= twice the previous element.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(m, int) or not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"m and n must be integers\")\n    if m < 1 or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"m and n must be positive integers\")\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n\n    # dp[v] stores the number of sequences of the current length starting with v.\n    # Use size m+2 for 1-based indexing and to avoid boundary checks.\n    dp = [0] * (m + 2)\n    for v in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[v] = 1  # For length 1, any value in [1..m] is valid\n\n    for _length in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Build suffix sums: suffix[v] = sum_{j=v..m} dp[j]\n        suffix = [0] * (m + 2)\n        for i in range(m, 0, -1):\n            suffix[i] = dp[i] + suffix[i + 1]\n\n        # new_dp[v] = number of sequences of this length starting with v\n        # where the next element is in [2*v .. m], so count = suffix[2*v]\n        new_dp = [0] * (m + 2)\n        for v in range(1, m + 1):\n            idx = 2 * v\n            if idx <= m:\n                new_dp[v] = suffix[idx]\n            else:\n                new_dp[v] = 0\n        dp = new_dp\n\n    return sum(dp[1 : m + 1])"}
