{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the given number n.\n    Assumes n is an integer for calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        base = 0\n    else:\n        # Calculate the integer square root of n.\n        base = math.isqrt(n)\n        # If the square of 'base' is not strictly greater than 'n', increment 'base'.\n        if base * base <= n:\n            base += 1\n\n    return base * base"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # msis[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i]\n    msis = list(arr)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                msis[i] = max(msis[i], msis[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # msds[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i]\n    msds = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                msds[i] = max(msds[i], msds[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # The maximum sum bitonic subsequence is max(msis[i] + msds[i] - arr[i]) for all i\n    # arr[i] is subtracted because it is counted twice (once in msis and once in msds).\n    max_bitonic_sum = msis[0] + msds[0] - arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_sum = msis[i] + msds[i] - arr[i]\n        if current_sum > max_bitonic_sum:\n            max_bitonic_sum = current_sum\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "import functools\n\n@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=128)\ndef lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest palindromic subsequence (LPS) for a given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming for efficient computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    n = len(s)\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All substrings of length 1 are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of length L from 2 to n\n    # L represents the length of the current substring (from i to j)\n    for L in range(2, n + 1):\n        # i is the starting index of the substring\n        for i in range(n - L + 1):\n            j = i + L - 1 # j is the ending index of the substring\n\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters at ends match, they can form part of the LPS.\n                # The length is 2 plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                # dp[i+1][j-1] is 0 if i+1 > j-1 (empty or invalid range) due to initialization.\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                # If characters at ends don't match, take the maximum of\n                # excluding s[i] (LPS of s[i+1...j]) or excluding s[j] (LPS of s[i...j-1])\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
