{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "def newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the Newman\u2013Shanks\u2013Williams number S_n (S_0 = 1, S_1 = 1, S_n = 2*S_{n-1} + S_{n-2}).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    def mat_mult(a, b):\n        return (\n            (a[0][0] * b[0][0] + a[0][1] * b[1][0],\n             a[0][0] * b[0][1] + a[0][1] * b[1][1]),\n            (a[1][0] * b[0][0] + a[1][1] * b[1][0],\n             a[1][0] * b[0][1] + a[1][1] * b[1][1]),\n        )\n\n    def mat_pow(mat, exp):\n        result = ((1, 0), (0, 1))  # identity\n        base = mat\n        while exp > 0:\n            if exp & 1:\n                result = mat_mult(result, base)\n            base = mat_mult(base, base)\n            exp >>= 1\n        return result\n\n    M = ((2, 1), (1, 0))\n    m = mat_pow(M, n - 1)\n    # S_n = m * [S1, S0] first component; S1 = S0 = 1 => S_n = m[0][0] + m[0][1]\n    return m[0][0] + m[0][1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "def dog_age(years: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in dog-years based on a common veterinarian approximation.\n    The first two calendar years count as 10.5 dog-years each; subsequent years count as 4 dog-years each.\n    \"\"\"\n    if years <= 0:\n        return 0.0\n    elif years <= 2:\n        return years * 10.5\n    else:\n        return 2 * 10.5 + (years - 2) * 4.0"}
