{"task_id": "Mbpp/267", "solution": "def square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the squares of the first n odd natural numbers.\n\n    Uses the closed-form formula:\n        sum_{k=1..n} (2k-1)^2 = n * (2n - 1) * (2n + 1) / 3\n\n    Args:\n        n: Number of first odd natural numbers.\n\n    Returns:\n        The integer sum of squares.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: if n is not an int.\n        ValueError: if n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\n    return (n * (2 * n - 1) * (2 * n + 1)) // 3"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(items, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists, distributing elements interleaved.\n    Each sublist contains elements where their original index modulo n is constant.\n    \"\"\"\n    partitions = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for index, item in enumerate(items):\n        partitions[index % n].append(item)\n    return partitions"}
