{"task_id": "Mbpp/281", "solution": "def all_unique(seq):\n    \"\"\"Checks if all elements in the given sequence are unique.\n    Uses a set for hashable elements (O(n) average) and falls back to pairwise comparison\n    for unhashable ones (O(n^2)).\n    \"\"\"\n    if seq is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input cannot be None\")\n    try:\n        iterator = iter(seq)\n    except TypeError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be an iterable/sequence\")\n\n    try:\n        seen = set()\n        for item in seq:\n            if item in seen:\n                return False\n            seen.add(item)\n        return True\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback for unhashable elements (e.g., lists within list)\n        n = len(seq)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                if seq[i] == seq[j]:\n                    return False\n        return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/279", "solution": "def is_num_decagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the nth decagonal number: D(n) = 4*n^2 - 3*n.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer\")\n    return 4 * n * n - 3 * n"}
