{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "from typing import Sequence, Tuple\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: Sequence[Tuple[int, int]], list2: Sequence[Tuple[int, int]]) -> set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of 2-element tuples between two lists, irrespective of tuple element order.\n    Each tuple is normalized to a canonical form (sorted elements) before set operations.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Normalize each tuple in the first list to a canonical form (e.g., (a, b) becomes (min(a,b), max(a,b))).\n    normalized_set1 = {tuple(sorted(t)) for t in list1}\n\n    # Normalize each tuple in the second list similarly.\n    normalized_set2 = {tuple(sorted(t)) for t in list2}\n\n    # Compute the intersection of the two sets of normalized tuples.\n    # The result is already in the desired canonical tuple format.\n    return normalized_set1.intersection(normalized_set2)"}
