{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "import heapq\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\n\ndef expensive_items(items: list[dict], n: int) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the n most expensive items in a list of dictionaries based on their 'price'.\n    Prices are compared using Decimal for precision.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _to_decimal(value) -> Decimal:\n        if isinstance(value, float):\n            value = format(value, \"f\")\n        return Decimal(str(value))\n\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    processed_items = []\n    for item_dict in items:\n        if 'name' not in item_dict or 'price' not in item_dict:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each item must have 'name' and 'price' keys\")\n        price_decimal = _to_decimal(item_dict['price'])\n        processed_items.append({'name': item_dict['name'], 'price_decimal': price_decimal})\n\n    if n >= len(processed_items):\n        sorted_expensive = sorted(processed_items, key=lambda x: x['price_decimal'], reverse=True)\n    else:\n        sorted_expensive = heapq.nlargest(n, processed_items, key=lambda x: x['price_decimal'])\n\n    result = []\n    for item_data in sorted_expensive:\n        result.append({\n            'name': item_data['name'],\n            'price': float(item_data['price_decimal'])\n        })\n\n    return result"}
