{"task_id": "Mbpp/792", "solution": "from typing import Sequence, Any\nfrom collections.abc import Sequence as ABCSequence\n\ndef count_list(container: Sequence[Sequence[Any]], validate: bool=False, strict_list: bool=True) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of immediate sub-lists within the given container.\n    By default, only instances of `list` are counted; other sequence types can be counted with `strict_list=False`.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    if strict_list:\n        for item in container:\n            if isinstance(item, list):\n                count += 1\n    else:\n        for item in container:\n            # Count any Sequence type that is not a string or bytes\n            if isinstance(item, ABCSequence) and not isinstance(item, (str, bytes)):\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index if found, otherwise returns -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1  # Initialize result to -1 (not found)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last occurrence\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1  # Target is in the right half\n        else:  # arr[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1  # Target is in the left half\n    return result"}
