{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of all odd natural numbers within the range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are positive integers starting from 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Adjust the lower bound to be at least 1, as natural numbers start from 1.\n    effective_l = max(l, 1)\n\n    # If the effective lower bound is greater than the upper bound, there are no numbers in the range.\n    if effective_l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the first odd natural number within the adjusted range [effective_l, r].\n    # If effective_l is odd, it's itself. If even, the next number (effective_l + 1) is odd.\n    first_odd_num = effective_l if (effective_l & 1) else effective_l + 1\n\n    # Determine the last odd natural number within the range [effective_l, r].\n    # If r is odd, it's itself. If even, the previous number (r - 1) is odd.\n    last_odd_num = r if (r & 1) else r - 1\n\n    # If the calculated first odd number is greater than the last odd number,\n    # it means there are no odd numbers in the effective range.\n    if first_odd_num > last_odd_num:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the count of odd numbers in the arithmetic progression.\n    # The common difference between consecutive odd numbers is 2.\n    count = (last_odd_num - first_odd_num) // 2 + 1\n\n    # Calculate the sum of the arithmetic progression.\n    # Sum = (number of terms / 2) * (first term + last term)\n    total_sum = (first_odd_num + last_odd_num) * count // 2\n\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(n, d):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit number `n` to the left by `d` positions.\n    The number `n` is treated as an unsigned 32-bit integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    WORD_SIZE = 32\n    MASK = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    n = n & MASK\n    d_mod = d % WORD_SIZE\n\n    if d_mod == 0:\n        return n\n\n    # Perform the left rotation: (n << d_mod) OR (n >> (WORD_SIZE - d_mod))\n    # The final MASK ensures the result remains within 32 bits.\n    return ((n << d_mod) | (n >> (WORD_SIZE - d_mod))) & MASK"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/798", "solution": "def _sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numeric elements in an array.\n    Returns an integer if all elements are integers (excluding booleans), otherwise a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine if all elements are strictly integers (excluding bools) to decide return type.\n    all_ints = all(isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool) for v in arr)\n\n    total = 0\n    for v in arr:\n        total += v\n\n    # Return the sum as an int if all elements were integers, otherwise as a float.\n    return int(total) if all_ints else float(total)"}
